  "interpretation": "<ul><li>A sickling test is used to diagnose sickle cell anemia, a genetic blood disorder that affects the shape of red blood cells. In sickle cell anemia, the red blood cells become rigid and curved, which can block blood flow and cause pain, organ damage, and other complications.<br></li><li>A positive result indicates the presence of sickle hemoglobin, which confirms a diagnosis of sickle cell anemia.&nbsp;<br></li></ul>",
